## Summary

This PR introduces `html` templating in InstantSearch.js.

This allows InstantSearch.js users to pass templates as HTML strings safely, with easier access to exposed data, and with an easier API to set up events.

[**Try this live**](https://codesandbox.io/s/instantsearch-js-forked-xfoouv?file=/src/app.js) | [**Read RFC**](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch-rfcs/blob/master/accepted/html-templating-instantsearch.md)

>The current sandbox needs to import `@babel/runtime` for now, this will be fixed.

```js
instantsearch.widgets.hits({
  // ...
  templates: {
    item(hit, { html, components, sendEvent }) {
      return html`<article>
        <h2>${components.Highlight({ hit, attribute: 'name' })}</h2>
        <p>${components.Snippet({ hit, attribute: 'description' })}</p>
        <button
          onClick="${() => sendEvent('conversion', hit, 'Product Added')}"
        >
          Add to cart
        </button>
      </article>`;
    },
  },
});
```

**Note:** For now, the feature doesn't work in [`pagination`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/pagination/js/) and [`geoSearch`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/geo-search/js/). `pagination` will be handled separately, and `geoSearch` will be tackled later (at most when we deprecate Hogan.js) depending on complexity and demand.

## Tests

Testing this feature involves testing templates in ~20 widgets. That's a lot of files, so I did it in a [separate PR](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/pull/5087).
